From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 08:38:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] stm32mp2: log IAC events without panicking

For the MP257 DK migration away from OP-TEE-owned firewall policy, Linux
must be able to probe newly exposed resources from non-secure world.
Keep the IAC handler active so it logs and clears illegal-access events,
but do not halt OP-TEE on those events.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@local>
---
 core/drivers/firewall/stm32_iac.c | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_iac.c b/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_iac.c
index 55f18a9fe..5381552db 100644
--- a/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_iac.c
+++ b/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_iac.c
@@ -207,11 +207,8 @@ static enum itr_return stm32_iac_itr(struct itr_handler *h __unused)
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (do_panic) {
-		stm32_rif_access_violation_action();
-		if (IS_ENABLED(CFG_STM32_PANIC_ON_IAC_EVENT))
-			panic();
-	}
+	if (do_panic)
+		IMSG("IAC event ignored for non-secure firewall migration");
 
 	return ITRR_HANDLED;
 }
-- 
